WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.942
The Department of Defense depends on a broad industrial base to design, build, operate, and support mission capabilities.

2
00:00:07.942 --> 00:00:15.605
Sensitive information often moves across organizational boundaries as many companies contribute to the same program or supply chain.

3
00:00:15.605 --> 00:00:19.048
A weakness at any participant can create wider risk.

4
00:00:19.048 --> 00:00:28.247
A small supplier may handle information that affects a major platform, while a service provider may support systems used by several contractors.

5
00:00:28.247 --> 00:00:32.498
Organization size alone does not determine information sensitivity.

6
00:00:32.498 --> 00:00:43.762
Cyber threats against the DIB can affect intellectual property, acquisition information, engineering data, operational capability, cost, schedule, and national security.

7
00:00:43.762 --> 00:00:49.190
Protecting unclassified information is therefore an important part of protecting defense missions.

8
00:00:49.190 --> 00:01:00.365
DoD contracts have long included safeguarding requirements, including requirements connected to FCI, CUI, and NIST SP 800-171.

9
00:01:00.365 --> 00:01:06.292
CMMC adds a formal verification framework around applicable cybersecurity expectations.

10
00:01:06.292 --> 00:01:15.262
Verification helps the government and contracting community distinguish between a stated policy and a practice that is implemented within a defined environment.

11
00:01:15.262 --> 00:01:21.388
It creates common terminology for levels, assessments, findings, affirmations, and status.

12
00:01:21.388 --> 00:01:24.691
CMMC also supports supply-chain accountability.

13
00:01:24.691 --> 00:01:38.350
Requirements may affect subcontractors when protected information or covered contract work flows to them, so prime contractors and suppliers need clear communication about information, systems, and responsibilities.

14
00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:44.157
The program is intended to improve consistency, but it does not make every contractor identical.

15
00:01:44.157 --> 00:01:51.421
The required level and assessment type are determined by current program rules and the applicable solicitation or contract.

16
00:01:51.421 --> 00:01:58.266
CMMC cannot eliminate cyber threats or guarantee that an organization will never experience an incident.

17
00:01:58.266 --> 00:02:06.577
Its value is stronger implementation, clearer accountability, and greater confidence that protected information receives required safeguards.
